WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:08.860
Quelana: "My mother, the Witch of Izalith, was one of the primeval lords."

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.360
Quelana: "Her power came from a soul that she found near the First Flame."

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.220
Quelana: "She focused this power to light a flame of her own,"

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.100
Quelana: "but she failed to control it..."

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.120
Quelana: "The Flame of Chaos.. Engulfed mother and my sisters,"

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.500
Quelana: "and molded them into deformed creatures."

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.840
Quelana: "Only I escaped, and now I'm here."

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.020
Quelana: "My mother..."

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.020
Quelana: "My sisters..."

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:38.240
Quelana: "What have you done?"

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.220
Long ago , we thought the Chaos Flame was born of desperation

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.980
a flame created to replace the fading First Flame ,

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.300
and to secure the age of fire for the Lords,

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.100
we were wrong.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.260
Izalith's flame was a flame of ambition,

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.960
for the First Flame gave life, and Izalith believed that her soul could replicate this power...

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.400
...and she was right.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.240
But, not in the way that she expected

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.840
For when the witch and her seven daughters huddled together

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.040
and focused their power, chaos was born.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:20.660
Their flame spiraled out of control,
engulfing the women and the city of Izalith

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:23.360
And during this period of instability,

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.780
the very worst demons were born.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.080
But soon after, the witch clearly wrested chaos under control,

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.860
becoming the Bed of Chaos and the heart of a new city.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.880
On that day, Izalith learned a set of core truths.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.420
First, that her power has limits.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.660
Second, that fire is to be feared.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:47.620
And third, that grotesque, parasitic life...

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.100
...is still life.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.720
The first daughter we meet is Qualaag.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.180
She's described by her soul as a perfect creation of Chaos,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.420
and we see this in her movements.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.740
Note how she affectionately caresses her demon half,

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.680
how she smiles with contentment,

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.680
and how she embraces her parasite.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.380
Quelaag: "Ah. A precious new sacrifice."

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.660
Quelaag: "The Children of Chaos are hungry. Give yourself to Qualaag's flame."

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.220
A steady stream of undead are attempting to ring the second bell of awakening,

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:28.780
making this the perfect place for a Daughter of Chaos to nest.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:33.600
For Chaos, just like the First Flame, thrives off of humanity.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.240
Quelaag: "Those who defy the pact,"

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.000
Quelaag: "those who trespass Qualaag's domain,"

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.740
Quelaag: "may you feel the depth of our wrath."

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:47.360
She speaks of a pact, but a clueless undead can have no knowledge of this.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:51.020
To us, Qualaag is just another foe who blocks our path...

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.360
...but she was so much more than that.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.560
Eingya: "Oh dear."

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.540
Eingya: "What have we here? Are you a new servant?"

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.040
Eingya: "Hmph, but... You have no eggs."

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:12.100
Eingya: "Ah, no matter. Go along and have audience with our Fair Lady."

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:19.840
Eingya: "Except, If you lay a hand on the Fair Lady, you should be prepared to face my wrath."

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.260
The Fair Lady: "Qualaag,"

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.400
The Fair Lady: "my dear sister,"

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.380
The Fair Lady: "what is it?"

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.400
The Fair Lady: "Don't mind me... it does not hurt terribly."

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.800
The Fair Lady: "Your visits are more than anything."

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.580
The Fair Lady: "I'll be fine."

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.720
The Fair Lady: "I have you, dear sister."

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:49.280
The Fair Lady: "But promise me that you will take care of your self."

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:55.260
The Fair Lady is second Daughter of Chaos we meet, but she's not much longer for this world.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:04:00.920
Blind, ailing, and unfeeling, she subsists on offerings of humanity.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.320
Humanity that her sister Qualaag once brought to her.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:10.400
With the Old Witch's Ring in our possession, the Fair Lady understands us.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.400
And since Qualaag was the only remaining one capable of speaking to her,

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.080
you must be her sister.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:29.520
The Fair Lady: "You know, I still remember your beautiful, silky face. If only I could gaze upon it once more."

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.040
The Fair Lady: "Is something troubling you?"

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.520
The Fair Lady: "Please sister, do not cry."

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.800
The Fair Lady: "I am happy, really."

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.160
The Fair Lady: "I-I have you,"

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.880
The Fair Lady: "don't I?"

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.200
Eingyi: "You speak the tongue of the Fair Lady?

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.180
Eingyi: "In all honesty,"

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:58.340
Eingyi: "I am envious. What comfort can I offer without speaking her tongue?"

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:02.020
This egg-burdened undead was once an renowned Pyromancer.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.900
He developed spells of toxic and poisoned mists,

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.480
which are considered to be terrible, heretical spells.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.220
These pyromancies earned him exile,

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.220
followed by a terrible infection,

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:17.760
and then led to a chance meeting with the Daughter of Chaos.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.300
Eingyi: "Worse than undead,"

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:25.940
Eingyi: "we are diseased, and unwanted, like the grime of the Great Swamp."

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.780
Eingyi: "But my dear Fair Lady,"

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.380
Eingyi: "she cried for me, and swallowed the great blight pus,"

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.780
Eingyi: "despite mistress Qualaag's orders to the contrary."

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.620
These two Daughters of Chaos care really deeply about their offspring,

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:47.740
And, in the Fair Lady's case, even for the undead that carry those offspring.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:51.340
But without the humanity that her sister brought her,

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.420
she, and her children,

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:54.540
will die.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.600
The Fair Lady: "Q-Qualaag, my dear sister,"

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.640
The Fair Lady: "the eggs, it hurts..."

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.220
The Fair Lady: "They've gone still. I am afraid..."

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.880
The Fair Lady: "It may be too late."

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:14.160
The Fair Lady: "I am so sorry, dear sister."

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:19.520
Luckily, Eingyi does not yet know that mistress Quelaag... is dead.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:25.000
So, he shares his flame with you, which is a deeply personal act for a Pyromancer,

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.380
because the flame is a part of himself.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.940
Eingyi: "You have served our Fair Lady well."

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:35.020
Eingyi: "Now, let this strength be yours."

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:39.240
Before there were pyromancies, there were fire sorceries.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:43.980
And then, when the Witch of Izalith shared her flame with her daughters,

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.580
Pyromancy came to be.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:49.780
Unlike Sorcery, which requires a certain intellect,

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.160
pyromancy is this personal, primal art,

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:57.020
rooted in this desire to hold and control fire.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:02.300
And then, it's refined by the acceptance that true control is impossible.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:07.720
Laurentius: "Pyromancy is the ultimate fantasy. We are born into dark, and warmed by fire."

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.760
Laurentius: "But this fire, we cannot touch. "

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:13.000
Laurentius: "Those whose... fascination with fire persists,"

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.340
Laurentius: "learn to hold it in their own hand."

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:19.940
And so, humanity took really well to this ancient art,

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.200
passing down knowledge from a Daughter of Chaos herself.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:31.080
Eingyi: "Have you heard of Lost Quelana, an inhuman witch who wanders the poison swamp?"

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:36.680
Eingyi: "Only no one has ever seen her, so who really knows?"

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:39.780
Eingyi: "But what if she is another of the Quelaag sisters?"

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:44.080
Eingyi: "Our fair lady would be greatly comforted by her presence."

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.820
Quelana: "Hmm... A mere undead,"

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.260
Quelana: "Yet, you can see me."

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:55.600
Quelana: "Fascinating... I am Quelana, of Izalith. I am not often revealed to walkers of flesh."

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:00.960
Quelana: "You have a gift. Are you, too, one who seeks my pyromancy?"

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:04.440
Quelana is the eldest Daughter of Chaos,

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:06.780
and she's the furthest one from home.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:11.000
It's thanks to her that mankind became so attuned to pyromancy.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:15.040
Quelana: "Pyromancy is the art of invoking and manipulating fire,"

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.760
Quelana: "But remember one thing..."

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.260
Quelana: "Always fear the flame,"

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:22.100
Quelana: "lest you be devoured by it, and lose yourself."

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.120
Quelana: "I would hate to see that happen again."

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:30.000
Interestingly, Quelana refuses to teach the Chaos pyromancy of her homeland,

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:34.720
instead, opting for the more refined pyromancies to come:

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:39.100
Fire Whip. An effort to control that which cannot be controlled.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:43.960
Fire Storm, which desplays the indiscriminate horror of flame.

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:47.940
And, perhaps most importantly, Rapport -

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:52.380
an advanced spell of Quelana that uses fire to lure the living,

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:54.600
making them a temporary ally.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:57.580
Quelana: "Hm."

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:59.500
Quelana: "I have a favor to ask."

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:04.320
Quelana: "I abandoned my mother and sisters, and fled to this land."

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.600
Quelana: "But my mother and sisters have been in anguish since."

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.560
Quelana: "I beseech you,"

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:12.740
Quelana: "free mother and my sisters from the Flame of Chaos."

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:15.080
Quelana: "I cannot do it myself."

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:18.260
Quelana: "I lack the strength... and the bravery."

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.400
Quelana: "But you... I realize what I am asking, but please..."

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.860
Quelana: "free their poor souls."

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.220
Quelana: "Mother's ambitions were misguided, no doubt,"

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.900
Quelana: "but surely a thousand years of atonement is enough."

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:36.740
Quelana believes her family has been in penance for a thousand years,

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:39.360
and that death would be their only comfort.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:40.820
But is this true?

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:45.400
Will you take the word of a woman who's afraid to face her own demons?

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.760
The Flame of Chaos is not as evil as Quelana would have you believe.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:55.700
How could it be when it motivated an entire developed civilization?

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:59.060
Izalith's architecture is inspired by Chaos.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:02.080
Its first demons are considered priests.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:05.280
The Capra is capable of taming animals.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:10.260
There were embers of Chaos used for smithing, there is a written language, a spoken language -

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:13.900
This is not really a place that was ruined because of Chaos.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:16.460
It's a place that became defined by it.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:19.220
And it's all thanks to Mother Izalith.

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:24.060
If it was Izalith's goal to create a flame of life, then she succeeded,

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:29.700
for two younger sisters, and their mother, can be found in the depths of Izalith at its lowest point,

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.540
where demons are born.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:35.140
This seedbed of life is called the Bed of Chaos

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.100
It's actually comprised of three family members.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:44.580
Flanking on the sides are two enchanted, fleshy mounds connected to the center with staves.

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:51.320
Staves that look awfully like the Izalith staff seen in the beginning, where two sisters flank the mother in the center.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.300
Which makes the center of the Bed of Chaos...

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:56.240
Mother Izalith herself.

00:10:56.620 --> 00:11:00.800
Her control is evident by virtue of our ability to undo it:

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:05.600
Because if you take out a Sister on the side, then the Heart of Chaos breaks free.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:09.020
So, if Chaos was under control,

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:11.100
what happened to Izalith?

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.620
Well, war.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:17.460
Despite Izalith's aide in Gwyn's war against the dragons,

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.920
the Lord of Light turned his ire to the creatures of Chaos.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.580
Did he feel threatened by these monsters?

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:28.860
Did he consider Chaos to be this affront to the integrity of Divine Flame?

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:30.920
It's impossible to say for sure.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:36.220
For this war, he commissioned an elite order of warriors who became known as the Black Knights.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:40.820
Their oversized weapons were designed to deal with their oversized foes,

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:47.360
And their loyalty to Gwyn was so fierce that they would later follow him into the Kiln of the First Flame.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:54.800
If there ever was a time for Quelana to slip away and leave,

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:57.480
it would be now, during the war.

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:01.280
Her family must have thought that she died.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:02.540
For upon an alter,

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.000
dressed upon an unrecognizable corpse,

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:10.120
is a gold-hemmed set that says it was once worn by Quelana of Izalith.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:13.820
So, not only does this suggest that she faked her death...

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:18.680
it suggests that she couldn't bear to have her family know about her desertion,

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.440
and this news,

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:21.800
of her death,

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:25.040
would have hit no one harder than her brother.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.820
This giant is a being of Ceaseless Discharge,

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:33.820
born alongside the worst demons when the Chaos Flame was still unstable

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:41.540
So, to soothe his lava inflamed sores, his witch sisters gave him a special Orange Charred Ring.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.920
Which, fool that he is,

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.320
he accidentally dropped.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.980
He would never receive another.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:50.500
And so he spent the rest of his days in pain,

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:53.320
oblivious to everything around him.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:56.960
Everything, except the shrine to his sister Quelana.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:01.640
Desecrate her corpse, and he would literally throw away his life to punish you.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:04.620
So strong is the love for his family.

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:35.620
Leaving her family may well have been the worst decision Quelana could have made.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.960
For, in a move that she could not have predicted,

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:42.980
Gwyn stopped short of annihilating the demons entirely.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.160
Izalith, after all, was already broken

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:50.640
referred to by many as "the Obsolete Capital of Chaos."

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.940
In return for their miserable lives,

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:55.780
and along with a promise to never leave Izalith,

00:13:56.140 --> 00:14:01.180
it appears that Gwyn received a swarm of demonic troops for his own army.

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:03.240
Stray demons guard the Asylum,

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:06.900
Lesser bat-wing demons became the messengers of the gods,

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:11.980
And a white-winged, demonic lion watches over the sanctuary of Oolacile.

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:15.560
So it was that the Family of Chaos survived.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:18.380
And Quelana deserted them all.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:22.480
It's likely Quelana didn't expect her sisters to survive the war,

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:27.380
but now that they have, she becomes stuck in this awkward state of Limbo.

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:31.800
She cannot return, for she disgraced and abandoned her family.

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:36.860
And yet, nor can she bring herself to fully leave, either.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:40.460
Instead, she sits as close to Chaos as possible,

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:45.660
punishing herself with this endless wandering through a poison swamp

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:49.640
She watches on, so close to her tormented family...

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:53.940
And yet, given her survivor's guilt, and her cowardice,

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:55.940
she might as well be miles away...

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:02.060
Which is a shame, because Quelana could truly be a comfort to her remaining family.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:03.760
Especially to the Fair Lady,

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:05.160
to her brother,

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.340
and to her mother.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:10.640
Quelana: "The Witch of Izalith... Please, do not speak of her."

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.440
Quelana: "I abandoned my mother and sisters,"

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:15.240
Quelana: "And fled to this land."

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:21.000
Quelana: "Now I roam these parts feigning ablution, and pretending to seek answers."

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:26.300
Finally, after a thousand years of survivor's guilt, she meets us.

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:29.280
Someone who can finally break the stalemate.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.540
She lacks the strength,

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:32.080
And the bravery

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.440
And we have a Lordvessel to fill.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:38.360
Eingyi: "You- You would betray us?! I should have known!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.980
Eingyi: "Ah, my dear Fair Lady!"

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:44.240
Eingyi: "You are in danger!"

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.000
The Fair Lady: "Quelaag?"

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.200
The Fair Lady: "What was that?"

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:52.000
The Fair Lady: "Is something troubling you?"

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:53.520
The Fair Lady: "Ah!!"

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:56.020
The Fair Lady: "Quelaag? But..."

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.120
The Fair Lady: "Why...?"

00:15:58.280 --> 00:15:59.580
Eingyi: "Why- ah! You-"

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:00.940
Eingyi: "Monster!"

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:02.140
Eingyi: "The Fair Lady!"

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:05.040
Eingyi: "What have you done?! What have you done?!?"

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:08.780
Eingyi: "Ay-haa, ah-haa..."

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:12.340
They gave everything to wrest Chaos under control.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:14.180
They ignited a culture,

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:18.000
They displayed that they could control their parasites, and

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:21.240
even that having a parasite, at all, is a choice.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:23.060
A choice to serve Chaos.

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:24.700
And we undo it all.

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:27.820
We rip the sister's shackles from Chaos,

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:31.420
and despite the Mother's feeble attempts to

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:33.400
sort of swat us away,

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:37.260
we finally put an end to Mother Izalith herself.

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:44.860
Quelana: "Outstanding - you have done very well."

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:46.200
Quelana: "Thank you."

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:48.500
Quelana: "I am blessed to have met you."

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:50.660
Quelana: "Please, take this."

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:52.680
Quelana: "It is all of me."

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:56.200
We fed Quelana's ignorance.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:59.620
She never got to see her brother mourn her for centuries.

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:05.200
She likely never knew that her sister poisoned herself for the good of the wretched.

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:07.760
Did she know that a Dark Wraith

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:11.060
was squirreling away humanity for his Fair Lady?...

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.000
That her mother

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:17.320
was doubled over in pain for centuries to contain Chaos?...

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:21.480
Survivor's guilt is a real traumatic condition,

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:24.280
and it led to the death of her family.

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:28.840
Aeons afterwards, the affects of all of this are still felt

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:34.100
Without the Mother, Chaos rises again, unbridled in a city called Eleum Loyce.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.640
Until a powerful King and Queen

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:39.680
sacrifice themselves to contain it once again.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:41.520
And even later still,

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.340
towards the end of the world,

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:46.360
surrounded by mountains of dead demons,

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:53.640
an Old Demon King gives up the Vestiges of Chaos in one final effort to fight for his species.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:57.560
There is only one silver lining to this tale.

00:17:57.920 --> 00:18:01.120
It's that deep within the long forgotten ruins,

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:05.340
past the last surviving off-shoots of the demon race,

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.720
and behind an illusory wall...

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:10.060
lies the corpse of Quelana,

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.320
curled up to the Fair Lady.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:15.820
She finally found the strength to return home.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:23.680
